# The passage of time, the Prologue's Scene 7 (#187), short for now. Played
# by your bunk (Bedside) when you sleep after the deck talk: the night passes
# in the dark, and it's the next morning. The rain has all but stopped, the
# Grave of the Lanterns' glow falls behind, the lantern flits about the deck
# brighter than he's been, and the captain studies the old chart. Then the
# lantern sees something ahead.
#
# It ends in the dark with the game going to the cove (@travel), where the
# arrival plays (arrival.dlg). The fuller montage (a clear turquoise sea,
# flying fish) is to come.

~ start
@fade out 0.0
@title The next morning
@rain 0.05
@grave on
@shot astern cut
@fade in 3.0
@wait 2.5
@grave off
@wait 3.0
@place lantern lantern_flight_1
@look lantern pleased
@shot about_the_deck cut
@wait 0.6
@go lantern lantern_flight_2
@wait 1.6
@go lantern lantern_flight_3
@wait 1.8
@place heron chart_reading
@shot at_the_chart cut
@wait 2.8
@place lantern the_bow
@shot the_lookout cut
@wait 1.2
lantern: Captain?
@shot at_the_chart cut
heron: Hm?
@shot the_lookout cut
@look lantern surprised
lantern: Look!
set arriving
@fade out 2.0
@travel cove
